{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1234905-how-to-make-the-fae-necromancer","id":1234905,"title":"How to make the Fae Necromancer","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-07-14T04:00:36-07:00","id":1234905,"title":"How to make the Fae Necromancer","content":"So - one of the things that I'm considering doing is trying to build a necromantic type of fae. Of course, there are a few tricks that are fairly obvious - looking at Sluagh as a kith option for one, as well as the Art of Autumn - but neither of these really captures a complete experience. I'm looking to make an entity who is willing to kill someone, just to raise them up again as a suitable soldier in service to him - the kind of person who takes a dragon and kills it to make a Dracolich. <br /> <br /> I've considered making a new custom art to reflect this kind of power if necessary (possibly most commonly found among dauntain, especially warlocks) - or treasures, or random mysterious chimerical powers to make the kinds of effects necessary to manage this. But I am a little curious if one thinks these kinds of necromantic tendencies are possible with what is already in the books - and what tricks you might take for someone who wanted to raise their army of the dead, using what spheres (with what realms). I've considered toying with things like, say, using Protocol with the Prop realm (targetting a corpse), but am curious to hear ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T04:19:40-07:00","id":1234908,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m thinking of different ways to do it for each Fae type. So we already Have Autumn Unleashings but I\u2019m thing we need an art of Spiritcraft or somesuch.<br /> <br /> For the Inanimae I have plans to develop an Osseus splinter.<br /> <br /> For the Hsien I\u2019m working on Yue Tan or Moon Alchemy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T05:56:16-07:00","id":1234922,"title":"","content":"Metamorphosis 1 can plausibly give a corpse a very, very basic type of life, by which I mean movement. It will still be a corpse in every other sense and you'd need Primal 1 to communicate with it, but for a very basic shambling zombie it could work.<br /> <br /> If you don't go for Primal, Naming 2 could also work. Giving a shambling corpse the nickname of &quot;Hallway patroller&quot; would cause it to mindlessly shamble up and down your hallway with no clear intent. Maybe add some kind of other effect to it with Time 3 so that, for example, when it encounters an enemy, creepy shadows surround it and start reaching for the intruder. Completely harmless but likely to make the intruder make a mistake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13395-daniel-knight","name":"Daniel Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T06:05:53-07:00","id":1234923,"title":"","content":"Chronos 3 is very useful for long term zombies, especially in hot climates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T10:01:07-07:00","id":1234992,"title":"","content":"Ironically, Spring might be a way to go to reanimate bodies. If the soul is gone, there is just the shambling corpse left. Perfect clay to mold.<br /> Probably a combination of all the Arts mentioned would be perfect. These are the things you probably want to go for in the long run. As for Realms, I'd suggest Nature/Actor and Prop to be highest, depending how your ST rules how you can influence dead bodies. Prop is for &quot;enhancements&quot; you want to make on the bodies, like fusing them with some armor and weapons or useful tools for your housekeeper zombies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T10:20:48-07:00","id":1234996,"title":"","content":"Crafting, no I am serious. If I kill a Dragon chimera and want a Dracolich chimera.. I make it from the Dragon parts(and other parts) bam Crafted Chimera. That's really the only way you're going to get intelligent undead outside just being lazy and just Sovereign geasing up a Wraith or Vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T10:51:07-07:00","id":1235007,"title":"","content":"Autumn unleashing and Sovereign is the way to go with rules as written! Naming and chronos for making them permanent servants, and include in some primal to make them burning skeletons or bind wind to corpse breath. Or metamorphoses to make them demonic half animals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T13:17:02-07:00","id":1235070,"title":"","content":"Autumn to summon Wraiths, or Spectres, and to lower the Shroud. Sovereign to command/control them.<br /> <br /> For creation of Chimerical undead, like with the Dragon example, I have to agree with Lian and say that Crafting is the best and most efficient way. If you insist on using Arts Naming might be able to do so and a generous ST might allow Metamorphosis to turn living thing into an undead thing but that is strecthing an already powerful Art. Also Oneiromancy can be used for creating undead Chimera by pulling such directly from the Dreams of dreamers, though this will get expensive fast.<br /> <br /> As for animati g Autumn corpses... well... there isn\u2019t a direct way. Spring can restore life hence it would be one generous ST that would allow for Awaken to awaken a dead being as Undead as it goes directly against the Arts themes. Autumn could summon a Wraith or a Spectre to possess the corpse, and it would need to be controlled through Sovereign. You could also use Legerdemain to puppet a corpse but it would be ridiculously expensive unless Unleashed. Again a really generous ST might allow for you to command the dead to rise through Sovereign but your have to convince him/her of it first.<br /> <br /> So necromancy as magic that would allow one to raise the dead of the Autumn world? Hard. Pretty much only Naming at 5th level or Unleashed would acallow for it.<br /> Necromancy as a Craft used to create Chimerical Undead? Well that is easily achievable through the crafting system.<br /> <br /> Naturally YMMV.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T15:33:06-07:00","id":1235096,"title":"","content":"I am trying to think if having access to immortal undead bodies would defeat the premise of the game. OR if that would make them even more prone to Banality..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-15T05:37:56-07:00","id":1235250,"title":"","content":"Of course, with Unleashing any solution can probably be created. I feel that Unleashing is sort of a Hammer in this solution, which is to say to use it the problem would be a nail. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1234905-how-to-make-the-fae-necromancer?p=1234996#post1234996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Crafting, no I am serious. If I kill a Dragon chimera and want a Dracolich chimera.. I make it from the Dragon parts(and other parts) bam Crafted Chimera. That's really the only way you're going to get intelligent undead outside just being lazy and just Sovereign geasing up a Wraith or Vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1234905-how-to-make-the-fae-necromancer?p=1235070#post1235070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For creation of Chimerical undead, like with the Dragon example, I have to agree with Lian and say that Crafting is the best and most efficient way. If you insist on using Arts Naming might be able to do so and a generous ST might allow Metamorphosis to turn living thing into an undead thing but that is strecthing an already powerful Art. Also Oneiromancy can be used for creating undead Chimera by pulling such directly from the Dreams of dreamers, though this will get expensive fast.</div> </div> </div> </div>While one might consider this viable, I'm not a hundred percent sure - one might have an easier time actually with the cumbersome processes of legerdemaine than this - mostly because (assuming your ST permits the creation of Sentient Chimera as Forged Chimera) each roll involved in this process is going to take a week - hardly something that's a viable tactic for your necromancer in this case.<br /> <br /> The Onieromancy though, that's expensive but it is an interesting thought. Think with a little bit of scene and the right set of tormented dreamers that might be viable tactic for our sorcerer, even if its not strictly the undead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1234905-how-to-make-the-fae-necromancer?p=1235096#post1235096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am trying to think if having access to immortal undead bodies would defeat the premise of the game. OR if that would make them even more prone to Banality..</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, this thought is very similar to my own. While I don't consider the idea of the undead to be antithetical to the premise of the game, I'm not sure that someone using a power would call their powers dark in the same like as one sees the Unseelie, or Dark in the same light as one sees that which is banal and destructive to the Dreaming. I've toyed with developing an art using both ideas - one that tries to fill in a necromantic niche that Autumn doesn't quite get, but is still very much 'fae' and 'dreaming', and an alternative which handles death as a banal process and is the kind of thing you might find a Warlock Dauntain learning in order to expand their power. Thinking if I go the banal process I might call it the Art of Denial (one of the abilities being &quot;to deny death&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T08:19:34-07:00","id":1235566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1234905-how-to-make-the-fae-necromancer?p=1235250#post1235250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While one might consider this viable, I'm not a hundred percent sure - one might have an easier time actually with the cumbersome processes of legerdemaine than this - mostly because (assuming your ST permits the creation of Sentient Chimera as Forged Chimera) each roll involved in this process is going to take a week - hardly something that's a viable tactic for your necromancer in this case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Making a Dracolich or any other Sapient Undead for your average Necromancer in fiction isn't something you do on the fly. It takes time! This is why I specify it for sapient undead types. I mean no one expects you to &quot;snap your fingers and get Frankenstien's monster&quot; right?<br /> <br /> Now if you need a hoard of ZOmbies fast, that's a different thing but those are two very different directions for the Necromancer and should require different qualities.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You know, this thought is very similar to my own. While I don't consider the idea of the undead to be antithetical to the premise of the game, I'm not sure that someone using a power would call their powers dark in the same like as one sees the Unseelie, or Dark in the same light as one sees that which is banal and destructive to the Dreaming. I've toyed with developing an art using both ideas - one that tries to fill in a necromantic niche that Autumn doesn't quite get, but is still very much 'fae' and 'dreaming', and an alternative which handles death as a banal process and is the kind of thing you might find a Warlock Dauntain learning in order to expand their power. Thinking if I go the banal process I might call it the Art of Denial (one of the abilities being &quot;to deny death&quot;) </div> </div> </div>The world does have ghosts, vampires, mummies etc but in theirown little setup<br /> <br /> But more than that if you want to become a Fairy &quot;lich&quot; it needs to have serious downsides, and I&quot;m not sure that the ones I can think of won't overlap with Lost Ones. I mean if you can't really leave a freehold without falling apart you aren't much different than a Lost one. OF course perhaps some Archdautain equivalent might exist...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-14T16:52:10-07:00","id":1254352,"title":"","content":"How would you travel to the Shadowlands? The closest thing I can think of is Wayfare 3 Portal Passage and use a combination of Actor and Fae Realms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The only consistent wisdom is in knowing you know nothing&quot; ~ Socrates <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1197-imthestein","name":"Imthestein","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1197_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-15T18:15:00-07:00","id":1254661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imthestein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1234905-how-to-make-the-fae-necromancer?p=1254352#post1254352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would you travel to the Shadowlands? The closest thing I can think of is Wayfare 3 Portal Passage and use a combination of Actor and Fae Realms.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Find a Trod that goes there would be the Canon.<br /> <br /> I personally would allow &quot;combo arts&quot; maybe Portal passage.. and some level of Autumn?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-16T07:56:47-07:00","id":1254769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1234905-how-to-make-the-fae-necromancer?p=1254661#post1254661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Find a Trod that goes there would be the Canon.<br /> <br /> I personally would allow &quot;combo arts&quot; maybe Portal passage.. and some level of Autumn?</div> </div> </div> </div>Finding a Trod was my thinking, but I didn't think any specifically went to the Shadowlands. Don't they always go to the Dreaming or have I completely misunderstood Trods this whole time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The only consistent wisdom is in knowing you know nothing&quot; ~ Socrates <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1197-imthestein","name":"Imthestein","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1197_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-16T12:17:50-07:00","id":1254816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imthestein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1234905-how-to-make-the-fae-necromancer?p=1254769#post1254769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finding a Trod was my thinking, but I didn't think any specifically went to the Shadowlands. Don't they always go to the Dreaming or have I completely misunderstood Trods this whole time.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There are paths in the dreaming that lead to the SHadowlands(Dark paths), and paths that lead to the Middle Umbra(green paths)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-16T14:35:38-07:00","id":1254850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1234905-how-to-make-the-fae-necromancer?p=1254816#post1254816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> There are paths in the dreaming that lead to the SHadowlands(Dark paths), and paths that lead to the Middle Umbra(green paths)</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah thank you, I'll check that out then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The only consistent wisdom is in knowing you know nothing&quot; ~ Socrates <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1197-imthestein","name":"Imthestein","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1197_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-19T03:00:04-07:00","id":1255452,"title":"","content":"I think there is no real good way to make a necromancer from the arts on the book, except for Unleashing a lot. A new art would solve it, of course, but I think a Meta-Art would be better, like the Meta-Disciplines from Vampire:<br /> <br /> The Walking Non-Living [Autumn 4 + Sovereign 4]<br /> <br /> The Fae can command the dead to raise again and commands them to do his bidding. A Sluagh invokes raises from the grave the whole cemetery to fight her enemies. A Sidhe revives an raven to go keep an vigil around. A Nocker revives a carcass of a car to make a fast retreat.<br /> System: The fae cast a cantrip on the mortal remains of someone/something, and it returns to functionality. The Realm defines what will resurrect. If it is was a living being, like a Dragon corpse, a human skeleton or the remains of a parrot, it comes back to a form of life, being able to move and act as they would be able to in life, but having no memories or intelligence. They can fulfill simple mundane tasks, as cleaning, fighting, vigil, pilling, but any activity that is intellectually or socially challenging is beyond their capacity. They can communicate and understand in the language of the first word said to them (if the caster says anything during the casting of the cantrip, it counts as the language). If the effect is being used on a object, like a car with a broken motor, and old rusted train, or a smashed cell phone, it will start working again, even if without battery or fuel. The object will follow the orders of the caster, but has no intelligence to interact with the environment (you can order a car to accelerate, but it will do it in a straight line, smashing and hitting anything on the way). In the case of a cell phone or computer, that has information inside, it has only the basic functions, and no information is restored (the cellphone can make calls, the computer can do calculations, but you cant access old whatzap conversations or the files on the computer). The object must still have some resemblance of what it is suppose to be, even if in separated parts. The spell does not magically generate or substitute missing parts (a lungless skeleton cant talk, an armless zombie cant grab, a motorless car wont go anywhere), but as long as it keeps the semblance of the part, it will work. The affected has no living (or working) signals. More success increase time: 1 success - Glamour Minutes, 2 successes - 30 minutes, 3 success - 1:30 hours, 4 successes - 3 hours, 5 successes 6 hours. The effect ends next sunrise or sundown, independently of the suppose duration.<br /> <br /> Wyrd","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12934,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","user":"Manbat","date":". 09-19-2018, 06:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","name":"Manbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12934_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}